alue "9" :db/id 17592186477013} {:answer/id #uuid "85a2d72a-110b-5ef3-91a7-6c6ea19a612f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88" :db/id 17592186477014} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e87be2-7f84-5050-8450-0a88afe51a84" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186477017} {:answer/id #uuid "e45d5b04-882a-57f9-a42e-18c402ad7f7b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id 17592186477024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f507488-4595-522d-987d-9cb1830b28d4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id 17592186477012} :answer-field/id #uuid "fecfe7d0-ddbf-5842-ad10-352285c2f4d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186477025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "436cab40-c84e-51f6-a518-ef754e1d23e8" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(m+7)x+8n=9x+88\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $m+n?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $m$ and $n$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(m+7)x+8n=9x+88\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+7=9.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n8n=88.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $m=2$ and $n=11,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+n=2+11=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186477007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e054d18f-0abd-534e-af79-b4becb7e8af4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id 17592186477023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e054d18f-0abd-534e-af79-b4becb7e8af4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id 17592186477023} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf404ba6-be51-5d74-9701-f28660bc675d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186477019}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "475d1245-f209-5a1a-94d0-b61255568fb1" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+16)x+2t=7x+12\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ and $t$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $s+t?$\n\n$s+t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $s$ and $t$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+16)x+2t=7x+12\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n-s+16=7.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get\n\n$$\ns=9.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n2t=12.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=6.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $s=9$ and $t=6,$ we have\n\n$$\ns+t=9+6=15.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186477016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c305d1ca-2a7e-5395-b01d-7f73d8b68b81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id 17592186477020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c305d1ca-2a7e-5395-b01d-7f73d8b68b81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id 17592186477020} :answer-field/id #uuid "94e8a50e-ea95-52e9-9247-89cc6599449e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186477015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af3151d7-d56f-5c03-a92e-cf11481af995" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+15)x+4t=3x+4\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ and $t$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $s+t?$\n\n$s+t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $s$ and $t$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(-s+15)x+4t=3x+4\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n-s+15=3.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $s,$ we get\n\n$$\ns=12.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n4t=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=1.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $s=12$ and $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\ns+t=12+1=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186477018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e96ccbc-fae0-58bf-a260-8810e64e49c8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id 17592186477003} {:answer/id #uuid "6135c2cd-ed41-554f-a365-6407044708b9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id 17592186477008} {:answer/id #uuid "64867657-b42b-5877-a7b8-d5f08508e6f0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id 17592186477009} {:answer/id #uuid "7795fc96-bada-5d47-80e4-bcc20f479e5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id 17592186477011} {:answer/id #uuid "da276f27-55cf-5a27-b424-c537ddd7a3e8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id 17592186477022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e96ccbc-fae0-58bf-a260-8810e64e49c8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id 17592186477003} :answer-field/id #uuid "1685aded-b577-5ed8-90cf-3a8f75f8adf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186477004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bae891b2-2044-5361-b2ef-88211b0b3d9f" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(m+8)x+8n=19x+48\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ and $n$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $m+n?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $m$ and $n$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(m+8)x+8n=19x+48\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+8=19.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we have\n\n$$\n8n=48.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $n,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $m=11$ and $n=6,$ we have\n\n$$\nm+n=11+6=17.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186477021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29420e57-07ec-566d-b584-32e9a65019be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186477005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29420e57-07ec-566d-b584-32e9a65019be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186477005} :answer-field/id #uuid "74d8a1c6-b3bb-5405-b5c5-2de709852649" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186477010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2ad0a7a-e832-5a60-bb09-72e5ecf114bf" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n5tx+(1-m)=55x+4\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ and $m$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t+m?$\n\n$t+m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $t$ and $m$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n5tx+(1-m)=55x+4\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n5t=55.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=11.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we get\n\n$$\n1-m=4.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $t=11$ and $m=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\nt+m=11+(-3)=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186491998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "651c6521-6052-5754-9de3-5d4d268af61b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186491636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "651c6521-6052-5754-9de3-5d4d268af61b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186491636} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d5121d0-bbcc-54ac-a60e-be4b2f5b9f0d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186491902}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b724bdb-17d7-5012-9f30-50cac17a9c4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-288570" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(-t-2)x=x\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t?$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=-t-2,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n-t-2=1.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-t & =3 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186492000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1471cbdf-bc97-5a46-8981-7245c7bab5e0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186491495} {:answer/id #uuid "48935b84-81f3-595a-95e3-e1292918d6c1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186491590} {:answer/id #uuid "6e935aa1-98de-58bc-8f29-612955963de6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186491653} {:answer/id #uuid "7b157d25-3f29-59c7-994c-6b0e54448964" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186491670} {:answer/id #uuid "8b47ef80-7919-5404-a1ab-a8ded7329dca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186491692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b47ef80-7919-5404-a1ab-a8ded7329dca" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186491692} :answer-field/id #uuid "e746e60c-472a-557f-8568-6d42ae2542ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186491975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d18683e-9cdc-5535-b6a1-ea077ac9eff1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288426" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nI. $4x+2=4x+2$\n\nII. $-2x-1=-2x-1$\n\nIII. $3x+5=3x+9$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & =4x+2 \\\\ 4x+2-4x & =4x+2-4x \\\\ 2 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $4x+2=4x+2$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-1 & =-2x-1 \\\\ -2x-1+2x & =-2x-1+2x \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-2x-1=-2x-1$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5 & =3x+9 \\\\ 3x+5-3x & =3x+9-3x \\\\ 5 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186492013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b1fd794-f42b-5316-80e9-0698cb1f8b87" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a General Equation With Infinitely Many Solutions For Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024ebb29-e554-55b8-8568-3de971cf842b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186491452} {:answer/id #uuid "0b409fa8-7fa2-5333-b719-1bf09e74f752" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186491476} {:answer/id #uuid "52608292-aa25-53a5-a80a-a1687fff019e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186491611} {:answer/id #uuid "e4026fca-c4a4-58f0-adbe-16c380971427" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186491844} {:answer/id #uuid "f0569689-8bdd-5f6e-84ed-219724f09b06" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186491865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4026fca-c4a4-58f0-adbe-16c380971427" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186491844} :answer-field/id #uuid "9275af45-98fb-5d13-b62c-71ff39cdad22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186491940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4fff83f5-94fb-54ad-8709-ecc3c59291a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-288574" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(k+2)x+r=5x+3\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ and $r$ are constants. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $k+r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax+b=cx+d\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,c,$ and $d$ are constants. This equation has infinitely many solutions if \n\n$$\na=c\\,\\text{and}\\,b=d.\n$$\n\nTo determine the values of $k$ and $r$ such that the equation\n\n$$\n(k+2)x+r=5x+3\n$$\n\nhas infinitely many solutions, we equate the coefficients of $x,$ and we equate the constants:\n\n- Equating the coefficients of $x,$ we have\n\n$$\nk+2=5.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk=3.\n$$\n\n- Equating the constants, we get\n\n$$\nr=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $k=3$ and $r=3,$ we have\n\n$$\nk+r=3+3=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186492056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110719 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff4e9141-5743-55f1-a8be-3e28cb047eca" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Equations With Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122da567-888b-521d-ab93-2bdadd7b97a5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186491491} {:answer/id #uuid "2c757179-64e0-523b-afeb-d5bc0ad04d2e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186491543} {:answer/id #uuid "93ecc79a-c63b-50da-a503-9b6d8ce7074b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186491705} {:answer/id #uuid "ab75275b-5761-5361-ae34-c628459ca7b2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186491752} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb65399-285a-555c-b2e6-5f5e24676387" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186491807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c757179-64e0-523b-afeb-d5bc0ad04d2e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186491543} :answer-field/id #uuid "884fd6c3-8303-53d8-9178-3d82c6fc0a29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186491937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc8f5f5a-7e03-528b-a06c-bf3c3858a8c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288431" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has infinitely many solutions?\n\nI. $3x+4=3x+4$\n\nII. $x-5=x-2$\n\nIII. $2x+3=x+3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4 & =3x+4 \\\\ 3x+4-3x & =3x+4-3x \\\\ 4 & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $3x+4=3x+4$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & =x-2 \\\\ x-5-x & =x-2-x \\\\ -5 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =x+3 \\\\ 2x+3-x & =x+3-x \\\\ x+3 & =3 \\\\ x+3-3 & =3-3 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2x+3=x+3$ has the unique solution $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186549009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc56c0e-abb3-5e53-818e-6aa51cc4af57" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186548439} {:answer/id #uuid "36c25fee-f58b-5409-a5a6-477628433eda" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186548463} {:answer/id #uuid "5ade53e2-0afe-522f-a54b-d5db209e2043" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186548522} {:answer/id #uuid "6e3dbfdf-aa6d-5049-8e76-3fb7df01f4ed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186548560} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1a1e15-d44d-54e8-a331-6ddc82706537" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186548595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1a1e15-d44d-54e8-a331-6ddc82706537" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186548595} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27fc349-c24d-5039-a135-0c2dd2d434ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186548967}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61992611-6e48-5a2e-9a4c-b280b994c51d" :question/math-academy-id "q-288561" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(t+4)x=2x\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=t+4,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nt+4=2.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $t,$ we get\n\n$$\nt=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186549054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eab2015-3700-56bf-ac92-fd0a94f661e2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id 17592186548387} {:answer/id #uuid "598ab84f-b8ec-5739-8cb0-fcbd36abfb06" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186548519} {:answer/id #uuid "96f6e7b6-efcd-5a03-89c8-76e8676edae9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186548648} {:answer/id #uuid "987b69a0-afb9-52c1-b363-d34b352bfb3b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186548656} {:answer/id #uuid "f71c8c9c-cd96-5e6e-b046-0e4cdbb2a210" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186548847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987b69a0-afb9-52c1-b363-d34b352bfb3b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186548656} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0b4382-89cc-5b45-b568-d6f0542bad8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186548879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d6ec3c46-2316-5f98-be70-c232b5719be1" :question/math-academy-id "q-288560" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(r-7)x=-x\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=r-7,\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\nr-7=-1.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\nr=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186553489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c2e38d-b9ae-5469-80da-9fbdd71de470" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186553020} {:answer/id #uuid "4c2cbe8d-3e4b-5384-8b16-725c4463dd05" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186553034} {:answer/id #uuid "9c93cb76-4c56-5d96-8b69-8368ebaaeef1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186553187} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d7c1ac-66b2-5bec-8e54-ba134d4a8328" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186553257} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b558ea-14a4-554d-a74d-bad2d525c660" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id 17592186553363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c2cbe8d-3e4b-5384-8b16-725c4463dd05" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id 17592186553034} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b7c28ee-4474-52da-a1df-71e406689457" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186553417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "021c858c-ff29-5406-946e-12cf5966af05" :question/math-academy-id "q-288441" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n7mx=-14x\n$$\n\nwhere $m$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $m?$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=7m,\\,b=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n7m=-14.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $m,$ we get\n\n$$\nm=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186555761 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6cd2f04-e0d5-5df0-8e74-ea737501cdf8" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b03681d2-3f8d-5d5a-b665-08eb5334df77" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id 17592186555422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b03681d2-3f8d-5d5a-b665-08eb5334df77" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id 17592186555422} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8685c5a-c976-5c4d-ba32-65fdf5654aca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186555734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06a0435e-893d-5476-8004-8e6faf0aa039" :question/math-academy-id "q-288569" :question/problem "Consider the equation\n\n$$\n(4r-6)x=22x\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has infinitely many solutions, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=bx\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. If $a=b,$ then the equation has infinitely many solutions.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=bx.$ In this case, \n\n$$\na=4r-6,\\,b=22.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has infinitely many solutions if\n\n$$\n4r-6=22.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4r & =28 \\\\ r & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]] "items" [[17592186110372 {:db/id 17592186572816 :learner-task/_items {:db/id 17592186413004 :lea