he activity." :db/id 1045 :db/ident :activity/title :db/valueType {:db/id 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Entry point into the activity; must be a member of activity/steps. This ordinary ref adds no second ownership relationship. Application stopping rules may finish an attempt before every step is presented." :db/id 1046 :db/ident :activity/first-step :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional calendar deadline, such as an assignment due date. Distinct from a time limit measured after starting." :db/id 1047 :db/ident :activity/due :db/valueType {:db/id 25}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional course this activity belongs to, such as the school course assigning homework. References a course entity. Independent of the content targeted by activity/scope and assigned-problem/topic-coverage; does not restrict supporting topics to this course." :db/id 1048 :db/ident :activity/course :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional curriculum content targeted by this activity. Lessons and reviews target a topic; diagnostics may target a course, unit, module, or topic. Omit when scope is fully described by the selected content. Course affiliation belongs on activity/course; assignment problem coverage belongs on assigned-problem/topic-coverage. This ordinary ref preserves shared curriculum." :db/id 1049 :db/ident :activity/scope :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite estimate of the activity's total working time, including adaptive practice. Omit when calculated directly from step estimates." :db/id 1050 :db/ident :activity/expected-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite wall-clock limit for the whole activity, measured from the task's first start. Pausing does not extend this limit." :db/id 1051 :db/ident :activity/time-limit-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy activity-definition identifier. Captured taskId values belong on learner-task; do not substitute a topic or content ID." :db/id 1052 :db/ident :activity/math-academy-id :db/valueType {:db/id 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of the activity definition, independent of learner attempts." :db/id 1053 :db/ident :activity/id :db/unique {:db/id 38} :db/valueType {:db/id 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after a correct answer. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/id 1054 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-correct :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after an incorrect answer when no retry is taken. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/id 1055 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-incorrect :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity when the learner explicitly skips the presented question. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic. Unpresented questions do not take this branch." :db/id 1056 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-skipped :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional alternate step in the same activity taken when the learner accepts a retry after a submitted incorrect answer. Use a different question on the same topic at the same difficulty, distinguishable from the ordinary incorrect continuation. The completed retry replaces the original result for frontier placement; both presentations remain in history. The application offers the available retry without a timing gate; skips receive no retry. Omit this branch on the alternate step to allow only one retry." :db/id 1057 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-silly-mistake :db/valueType {:db/id 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id 35} :db/doc "Optional next sibling step under the same activity or multistep owner. The final inner step returns to the 